<p>I still use Kratky for my herbs and lettuce. My DWC system handles the tomatoes and peppers. They both work. Start with Kratky and upgrade when you hit its limits.</p>

<h2>Your Next Move</h2>

<p>The Kratky method is the cheapest, easiest way to start growing food without soil. For $15 you can test it. For $50 you can scale to a small kitchen garden that saves you $80/month.</p>

<p><strong>Do this now.</strong> Buy a wide mouth mason jar and a pack of basil seeds. While they ship, read our <a href="/posts/hydroponics-for-beginners">Hydroponics 101 guide</a> for the full picture on how hydroponics works. Then follow the step-by-step setup above.</p>

<p>You'll have your first harvest in 3 to 5 weeks. I still remember the first time I made pesto from basil I grew in a jar. That feeling doesn't get old.</p>

